From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Seabraid <seabraid@example.invalid>
Date: Sat, 1 Jan 2000 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 05/16] seabraid retier: helper publishes post-round residency;
 main refuses a round whose held[] contradicts its applied ops

held[] was written only at plan load, so after an applied SWAP main kept routing the displaced
expert to a helper that skips experts it no longer holds (rows silently dropped), and re-proposed
displacing it (21 of 47 rounds refused in the 2026-11-06 D7 arms).

The include/strata/seabraid/channel.hpp (and expert_spec.hpp) half of this change lives in Seabraid's
adapters/strata/wire, the wire's one owner; this patch keeps only the engine side.
---
 src/core/remote_experts.cpp | 13 +++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 13 insertions(+)

diff --git a/src/core/remote_experts.cpp b/src/core/remote_experts.cpp
index 50c3a7c58..89bd22dae 100644
--- a/src/core/remote_experts.cpp
+++ b/src/core/remote_experts.cpp
@@ -716,6 +716,19 @@ bool RemoteExperts::seabraid_retier(const seabraid::TierWireOp* ops, int32_t n,
         }
     }
 
+    // (4b) The bitmap just adopted must show what the round reported applied.  If it does not, the helper's held[]
+    // is stale and this engine is now routing experts to slots that no longer hold them -- say so loudly.
+    if (cells > 0 && bl_held_.size() == cells) {
+        uint8_t rr[seabraid::kTierMaxOps];
+        for (int32_t i = 0; i < n; ++i) rr[i] = i < got ? hd->tier_res[i] : (uint8_t) seabraid::kTierPending;
+        std::string why2;
+        if (!seabraid::tier_residency_consistent(bl_held_.data(), (int64_t) layers_present_.size(), n_expert_, ops, rr, n, why2)) {
+            bl_->bump_epoch();
+            err = "seabraid retier: helper residency is STALE after an applied round (" + why2 + ")";
+            return false;
+        }
+    }
+
     // (5) Only now move the epoch.  It advertises a placement this engine has already adopted, so a request
     // published after it cannot be describing the old one.
     bl_->bump_epoch();
